|---|---|---|
| Median performance | ✅ Faster | ❌ Slower |
| Worst-case guarantee | ✅ O(N log N) | ❌ O(N²) possible |
| Small-array optimization | ✅ Insertion sort | ❌ Unless manually added |
| Pivot selection | ✅ Robust (median-of-k) | ❌ Unless manually optimized |
| Cache/friendliness | ✅ Tuned by experts | ❌ Likely suboptimal |
| Correctness Assurance | ✅ Battle-tested | ❌ Bug-prone |
| Maintainability | ✅ Zero maintenance | ❌ Ongoing burden |
| Portability | ✅ Standard C++ | ⚠️ May vary by luck |

**Choose `std::sort`.** It is provably better in every practical dimension for this problem. The only scenario where a custom sort might win is if you:
